    "message": "fix(websearch): honour provider rate-limit resets, align retention, cover query text\n\nThree defects found auditing the web search stack against main.\n\nRate-limit cooldown ignored the provider. KeyPool benched every 429 for a\nfixed 60s while the shared HTTP helper never looked at response headers, so a\nkey that resets in one second sat idle for a minute and one needing an hour got\nhammered. Providers publish the reset on every 429. The parser for that already\nexisted for the LLM provider path; it now lives in core/rate_limit.py and both\ncallers share it, rather than websearch importing from providers/.\n\nRetention desynced the two analytics tables. One logical route writes one row\nto search_route_log but >=1 to search_log (an extra per fallback hop), so the\nattempt table hits max_rows first. Pruning both to the same row count left\nroutes summarising a window whose attempt detail was already gone, while the\ndashboard renders the two tables side by side as if they covered the same\nperiod. Routes are now trimmed to the window surviving attempts still cover.\n\nWEBSEARCH_LOG_CAPTURE_CONTENT did not cover the query. The setting exists so\noperators can stop persisting search content, but the query column was written\nverbatim in both tables regardless -- leaving the most readable part on disk\nafter opting out.\n\nVerification: new tests reproduce each defect and fail without the fix\n(retention window, query withholding, Retry-After parsing across\nretry-after/retry-after-ms/x-ratelimit-reset-*/HTTP-date, and the cooldown cap).\nFull suite passes except 14 failures that also fail on unmodified main -- 8 from\nreal API keys in the local environment leaking past test isolation, 6 from the\nPowerShell installer tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
